                <pb facs="0218" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg106"/>

                <head>Chapter II: April 5–May 31, 1935</head>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Ambassador Grew on Japanese-Soviet relations following liquidation of Soviet
                        interests in Manchuria; the Hirota program of “cooperation” with China and
                        improvement in trade relations; consolidation of Japanese control in
                        “Manchoukuo”; Japanese campaign to win over Siam; Chinese Ambassador Yen on
                        improvement in Chinese-Soviet relations, May 13; revival of pressure by
                        Japanese military for political changes in North China following raising of
                        Japanese Legation to status of Embassy</p>
                </quote>





































































